<title>UK: BT raises domestic line rental charge 3.6 pct.</title>
<headline>BT raises domestic line rental charge 3.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Telecommunications Plc said on Friday it would raise its line rental charges for residential customers to 26.62 stg per quarter from 25.69 stg previously, an increase of 3.6 percent.</p>
<p>BT said in a statement that quarterly line rental charges for business customers would rise to 42.12 stg from 41.13 stg previously, a rise of 2.4 percent.</p>
<p>The company said the new charges are effective from July 1.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
